  "change": {
    "disk_tier": "CANADA_SCRATCH_DISK_TIER=1. In idle time the coldest conversation snapshots get byte-exact copies on local NVMe (direct I/O, SHA-256 per 4 MiB chunk, written in 32 MiB slices). A snapshot with a copy is parked (its memory returns to the snapshot pool) instead of dropped when the cache evicts it; a later turn reloads it, checking every digest, when the read beats prefilling the tokens it saves (read rate 2,200 MB/s plus 30 ms, measured). A reload takes room only under the cache's own slot and byte limits. Files live in one directory per device, capped at 64 GiB, and are removed when the engine starts.",
    "full_serving_regions": "CANADA_SCRATCH_FULL_REGIONS=1, CANADA_SCRATCH_ELASTIC_REGIONS=1, CANADA_SCRATCH_REGION_LOOKAHEAD=16384. Up to four conversations decode together in regions sized for the full context. Region memory is mapped on demand from a reserved address range and given back when conversations leave; regions 1 to the highest occupied one stay mapped, because the index scorer reads key ranges that can span a gap region (an earlier build that unmapped gap regions faulted there)."
  },
  "unchanged": [
    "weights",
    "kernels and numeric code",
    "every other setting of s1599 (snapshot pool 8 GiB, 4 GiB floor, cache budgets, prefill widths)",
    "2350 MHz clock policy",
    "the response timing contract",
    "portable profile"
  ],
